d Heat Transfer, particularly where the Fluid Properties and Flow Fundamentals module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of pressure measurement, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'pressure measurement; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of pressure measurement, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer', 'Active'), ('KCR_000668', 'friction factor', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer', 'Technical Concept', 'A dimensionless factor used to represent wall-friction losses in internal pipe flow.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of friction factor within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer, particularly where the Internal Flow module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of friction factor, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'A dimensionless factor used to represent wall-friction losses in internal pipe flow. Within Internal Flow, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of friction factor within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer, particularly where the Internal Flow module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of friction factor, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'friction factor; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of friction factor, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable a