 of drag within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer, particularly where the External Flow and Boundary Layers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of drag, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'drag; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of drag, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer', 'Active'), ('KCR_000672', 'flow separation', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer', 'Technical Concept', 'Detachment of a boundary layer from a surface when an adverse pressure gradient causes near-wall flow to reverse or weaken.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of flow separation within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer, particularly where the External Flow and Boundary Layers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of flow separation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Detachment of a boundary layer from a surface when an adverse pressure gradient causes near-wall flow to reverse or weaken. Within External Flow and Boundary Layers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of flow separation within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer, particularly where the External Flow and Boundary Layers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of flow separation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'flow separation; Core consideration